One-Time Setup on the Office Computer
Step 1 — Install Node.js v22 (if not already installed)
Download from https://nodejs.org → choose v22 LTS

Step 2 — Clone the project from GitHub


cd "C:\Users\YourName\Documents"
git clone https://github.com/iamagolfer/golf-tournament.git golf-app
cd golf-app
npm run install:all
Step 3 — Create the start shortcut
The .bat file won't be there since it's outside the golf-app folder. Just run:


npm start
Daily Workflow (Both Computers)
When you START working — always pull first:


cd "C:\...\golf-app"
git pull
npm start
When you FINISH — always push:


git add .
git commit -m "describe what you changed"
git push
If you changed any frontend files, add the build step:


npm run build
git add .
git commit -m "describe changes"
git push
Important: The Database is NOT Shared
Each computer has its own local db/golf.sqlite file — it's excluded from git on purpose (you don't want test data mixing with real data).

Where	Database
Home computer	Local test data only
Office computer	Local test data only
Railway (live)	Real tournament data — this is the one that matters
So you can test freely on either machine without affecting the live app on Railway.

If You Edit on Both Computers Same Day
Always git pull before starting to avoid conflicts. Since you're likely the only developer, conflicts are rare — but pulling first prevents them entirely.